  "id": "COMPOUND:3020 - PROTEIN:6018",
  "verbalization": "Duvoglustat is implicated in a complex network of interactions that ultimately lead to the activation of BR serine/threonine-protein kinase 1. The evidence suggests that Duvoglustat acts as a target for multiple downstream molecules, including 3-(1S,2R-Dihydroxypropyl)-1,6,8-Trihydroxyanthracene-9,10-Dione and Methionyl-tRNA formyltransferase. These molecules are themselves targets of other compounds, but the direct link between Duvoglustat and BR serine/threonine-protein kinase 1 is established through a chain of targets that ultimately converge on this kinase. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Duvoglustat may influence the activity of BR serine/threonine-protein kinase 1 through indirect interactions, possibly by modulating the expression or activity of upstream targets. The evidence supports a role for Duvoglustat in regulating this kinase, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
